.Dd November 4, 2026
.Dt LS7A_RTC 4 loongarch64
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ls7a_rtc
.Nd Loongson LS7A real-time clock
.Sh SYNOPSIS
To compile this driver into the kernel, place the following line in your
kernel configuration file:
.Bd -ragged -offset indent
.Cd "device ls7a_rtc"
.Ed
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver provides the battery-backed calendar clock in the Loongson LS7A
chipset.
It initializes system time at boot and stores updated time through the
system clock framework with one tenth of a second resolution.
Alarm interrupts are not used.
.Pp
The driver attaches to ACPI devices with the identifier
.Li LOON0001
or FDT nodes compatible with
.Li loongson,ls7a-rtc .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr date 1 ,
.Xr acpi 4
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
driver first appeared in
.Fx 16.0 .
